/*  Blanks in functions and methods — `InstantiateFunction`, `InstantiateMethod`, `Unify`,
    `Disagreeing` and `FilledBodyRefused` in `TypeChecker.Functions.cs`, `SignatureBlanks`,
    `WithoutTemplates`, `WithFilledMethods` and the re-check at the end of `Check` in
    `TypeChecker.Core.cs`.

    ★ A function or method whose signature names a type nobody declared, at least twice, is a
    TEMPLATE: set aside, never checked itself. Each call fills it from its arguments — `echo` called
    on a number reaches `echo of number`, a copy with every blank replaced — and the call remembers
    which filling it reached (the `:Filled` mark on the call), because the re-check will meet the
    same call with the template gone.

    ★★ The fillings' BODIES are checked by a second, fresh checker, on the program with the
    fillings spliced in front and the templates taken out — as C# does. Everything else in it was
    already checked once, so what that pass refuses is a filled body; and a refusal there is
    reported at the call that made the filling, with the body's own refusal underneath.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// A method filled for one owner.
    Define object filling with (the text owner, the node method).

    /// The call that made a filling: where, what it reached, with what, and how.
    Define object origin with (the number line, the text name, the text filled-with, the text verb).

    /// `SignatureBlanks`: the unknown type names a signature writes at least twice, in order.
    Bind series of text to signature-blanks unto checker, given (the node statement):
        Define counts as a map from text to number.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Cast one's count-unknown-names on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1), counts).
        Done.
        Define returned as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        If cast is-nothing on (returned) is false, cast one's count-unknown-names on (returned, counts).
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each pair in counts, repeat:
            If the value of pair is greater than 1, insert the key of pair into names.
        Done.
        Return cast sorted-ordinally on (names).
    Done.

    /// `Unify`: matches a signature's type against an argument's, learning what each blank is.
    /// A shape it does not understand matches — the ordinary argument check is the authority there.
    Bind fact to unify, given (the node pattern, the node actual, the map from text to fact blanks,
            the map from text to node found):
        If pattern's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define arguments-given as cast field-of on (pattern, 2).
            If arguments-given's kind is "list" and the number of arguments-given's children is 0:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pattern, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in blanks) is not void:
                    Define already as the entry for name in found.
                    If already is not void, return cast same-type on (already, actual).
                    In found, the entry for name becomes actual.
                Done.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        If pattern's kind is not actual's kind, return true.
        For each wrapper in a series with ("SeriesType", "StashType", "VoidableType", "FailureType", "ChannelType",
                "ReadableStreamType", "WritableStreamType"), repeat:
            If pattern's kind is wrapper:
                Return cast unify on (cast field-of on (pattern, 1), cast field-of on (actual, 1), blanks, found).
            Done.
        Done.
        If pattern's kind is "MapType":
            Define keys-agree as cast unify on (cast field-of on (pattern, 1), cast field-of on (actual, 1), blanks, found).
            Define values-agree as cast unify on (cast field-of on (pattern, 2), cast field-of on (actual, 2), blanks, found).
            Return keys-agree and values-agree.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// `Disagreeing`: the first blank written in `pattern`, for the message.
    Bind text to disagreeing, given (the node pattern, the map from text to fact blanks):
        If pattern's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define arguments-given as cast field-of on (pattern, 2).
            If arguments-given's kind is "list" and the number of arguments-given's children is 0:
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (pattern, 1)).
                If (the entry for name in blanks) is not void, return name.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each inner in pattern's children, repeat:
            If inner's kind is not "atom":
                Define hit as cast disagreeing on (inner, blanks).
                If hit is not "", return hit.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// A copy of `shape` with each blank — an object type of that name, filled with nothing —
    /// replaced by what fills it. Every node is a fresh one.
    Bind node to filled-deep, given (the node shape, the map from text to node found):
        If shape's kind is "atom", return shape.
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            Define arguments-given as cast field-of on (shape, 2).
            If arguments-given's kind is "list" and the number of arguments-given's children is 0:
                Define filling-type as the entry for (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1))) in found.
                If filling-type is not void, return filling-type.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define copy as a new node { the kind shape's kind, the word shape's word, the children a series of node }.
        For each child in shape's children, repeat:
            Cast copy's add on (cast filled-deep on (child, found)).
        Done.
        Return copy.
    Done.

    /// What the blanks are, read off a call's arguments — the first `skip` of them being the
    /// receiver of a method called in the free form.
    Bind map from text to node or failure to read-blanks unto checker, given (the node template,
            the series of text blanks, the node call-args, the number receivers, the text name, the number at-row,
            the fact for-method):
        Define blank-set as a map from text to fact.
        For each blank in blanks, repeat:
            In blank-set, the entry for blank becomes true.
        Done.
        Define found as a map from text to node.
        Define formals as (cast field-of on (template, 3))'s children.
        Define supplied as a series of node.
        Define skipping as receivers.
        For each passed in call-args's children, repeat:
            If skipping is greater than 0, decrement skipping by 1.
            Otherwise, insert passed into supplied.
        Done.
        Define shared as the number of supplied.
        If the number of formals is less than shared, the shared becomes the number of formals.
        Define place as 0.
        While place is less than shared, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define actual as cast one's infer on (item place of supplied) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-none on (actual) is false:
                Define pattern as cast field-of on (item place of formals, 1).
                If cast unify on (pattern, actual, blank-set, found) is false:
                    If for-method:
                        Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' can't take two different types for the same blank",
                            "'{name}' uses one name in more than one place in its signature, so those places have to agree",
                            at-row, "call '{name}' with arguments that disagree",
                            "Pass values whose types line up, or write a separate method for the other shape.")).
                    Done.
                    Define held as (the entry for cast disagreeing on (pattern, blank-set) in found) but void is cast unknown-type.
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on (
                        "'{name}' can't take both a {cast type-words on (held)} and a {cast type-words on (actual)} for the same blank",
                        "'{name}' uses one name in more than one place in its signature, so those places have to agree",
                        at-row, "call '{name}' with arguments that disagree",
                        "Pass values whose types line up, or write a separate function for the other shape.")).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        For each blank in blanks, repeat:
            If (the entry for blank in found) is void:
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{name}' can't tell what '{blank}' is here",
                    "'{blank}' is a blank in '{name}', and nothing passed in says what fills it",
                    at-row, "call '{name}' without saying what '{blank}' is",
                    "The blank is worked out from the arguments, so it has to appear in one of them.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// `echo of number` — the template's name, then what fills each blank.
    Bind text to filled-name, given (the text name, the series of text blanks, the map from text to node found):
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert name into out.
        For each blank in blanks, repeat:
            Insert " of {cast type-words on ((the entry for blank in found) but void is cast unknown-type)}" into out.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// `'element' with number`, for the refusal a filled body earns.
    Bind text to filled-with, given (the series of text blanks, the map from text to node found):
        Define out as a chase.
        Define first-one as true.
        For each blank in blanks, repeat:
            If first-one is false, insert ", " into out.
            The first-one becomes false.
            Insert "'{blank}' with {cast type-words on ((the entry for blank in found) but void is cast unknown-type)}" into out.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// A filling, in scope where it is asked for.
    Bind void to bind-filled-function unto checker, given (the text filled, the node concrete):
        Cast one's bind-name on (filled, a new binding {
            the shape cast one's resolved on (cast function-type-of on (concrete)),
            the established-by cast named-reference on (filled),
            the line cast numeric on (cast field-of on (concrete, 7)), the permanent false, the module false,
            the depth 0, the parameter false }).
    Done.

    /// `InstantiateFunction`: the filling this call reaches, made if it is new.
    Bind text or failure to instantiate-function unto checker, given (the text name, the node call-args,
            the number at-row):
        Define template as (the entry for name in one's generic-binds) but void is cast listed.
        Define blanks as cast one's signature-blanks on (template).
        Define found as cast one's read-blanks on (template, blanks, call-args, 0, name, at-row, false) or pass the failure off.
        Define filled as cast filled-name on (name, blanks, found).
        If cast one's look-up on (filled) is not void, return filled.
        // Made already, out of sight from here — a body's scope is gone once the body is checked.
        Define already-made as the entry for filled in one's made-functions.
        If already-made is not void:
            Cast one's bind-filled-function on (filled, already-made).
            Return filled.
        Done.
        In one's origins, the entry for filled becomes a new origin {
            the line at-row, the name name, the filled-with cast filled-with on (blanks, found), the verb "call" }.
        Define concrete as cast with-field on (cast filled-deep on (template, found), 1, cast quoted on (filled)).
        Insert concrete into one's instantiated-functions.
        In one's made-functions, the entry for filled becomes concrete.
        Cast one's bind-filled-function on (filled, concrete).
        Return filled.
    Done.

    /// A method already filled for this owner, or void.
    Bind voidable node to filled-method-of unto checker, given (the text owner, the text name):
        For each each-filling in one's filled-methods, repeat:
            If each-filling's owner is owner and cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (each-filling's method, 1)) is name, return each-filling's method.
        Done.
        Return void.
    Done.

    /// `InstantiateMethod`: the filling of a method this call reaches, or "" for a method that left
    /// no blank — ordinary dispatch handles that one.
    Bind text or failure to instantiate-method unto checker, given (the text owner, the text member,
            the node call-args, the number receivers, the number at-row):
        Define template as the entry for "{owner}'s {member}" in one's generic-methods.
        If template is void, return "".
        If (the entry for owner in one's bundled) is not void:
            Return a failure (cast not-judged on ("filling a blank in a book's own member")).
        Done.
        Define blanks as cast one's signature-blanks on (template).
        Define found as cast one's read-blanks on (template, blanks, call-args, receivers, member, at-row, true) or pass the failure off.
        Define filled as cast filled-name on (member, blanks, found).
        If cast one's filled-method-of on (owner, filled) is not void, return filled.
        In one's origins, the entry for "{owner}'s {filled}" becomes a new origin {
            the line at-row, the name member, the filled-with cast filled-with on (blanks, found), the verb "call" }.
        Define concrete as cast with-field on (cast filled-deep on (template, found), 1, cast quoted on (filled)).
        Insert a new filling { the owner owner, the method concrete } into one's filled-methods.
        Return filled.
    Done.

    /// The filling a call reached, as its `:Filled` mark says — or "".
    Bind text to filled-mark, given (the node said):
        Define place as 0.
        Define marked as false.
        For each child in said's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If marked, return cast unquoted on (child).
            If place is greater than 4 and child's kind is "atom" and child's word is ":Filled", the marked becomes true.
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Which filling this call reaches, worked out before anything is resolved — and marked on the
    /// call, the first time, so the re-check meets an answer where it will not find the template.
    Bind text or failure to call-filling unto checker, given (the node said, the node callee, the node call-args,
            the number at-row):
        Define marked as cast filled-mark on (said).
        Define reached as "".
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference" and (the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)) in one's generic-binds) is not void:
            The reached becomes cast one's instantiate-function on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)), call-args, at-row) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if marked is not "":
            Return marked.
        Done.
        Otherwise if callee's kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define target as cast one's infer on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            If target's kind is "ObjectType":
                The reached becomes cast one's instantiate-method on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)),
                    cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 2)), call-args, 0, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        Otherwise if callee's kind is "VariableReference" and the number of call-args's children is greater than 0:
            Define first as cast one's infer on (item 1 of call-args's children) or pass the failure off.
            If first's kind is "ObjectType":
                The reached becomes cast one's instantiate-method on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (first, 1)),
                    cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)), call-args, 1, at-row) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
        Done.
        If reached is not "" and marked is "":
            Cast said's add on (cast atom on (":Filled")).
            Cast said's add on (cast quoted on (reached)).
        Done.
        If reached is "", return marked.
        Return reached.
    Done.

    /// `FilledBodyRefused`: a filled body's refusal, reported at the call that filled it.
    Bind text to filled-body-refused, given (the origin source, the text inner):
        If the first 12 characters of inner is "unsupported\t", return inner.
        Define body as inner.
        If the first 6 characters of inner is "error\t", the body becomes the characters from 7 to the end of inner.
        Define indented as a chase.
        Define first-line as true.
        For each line in body split by "\n", repeat:
            If first-line is false, insert "\n" into indented.
            The first-line becomes false.
            If line is not "", insert "  {line}" into indented.
        Done.
        Return "error\tThat doesn't work: '{source's name}' does not work when it fills {source's filled-with}.\nHere on line {source's line}, you're trying to {source's verb} '{source's name}' with those types.\n\nIts body is what refuses them:\n\n{indented converted to text}".
    Done.

    // ── The re-check ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `WithoutTemplates`: the program with every function template taken out, through pulls.
    Bind node to without-templates unto checker, given (the node statements):
        Define kept as cast listed.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "BindStatement" and (the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) in one's generic-binds) is not void:
                Skip.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement":
                Cast kept's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 2, cast one's without-templates on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)))).
                Skip.
            Done.
            Cast kept's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Return kept.
    Done.

    /// `WithFilledMethods`: each object's template methods taken off and its fillings put on.
    Bind node to with-filled-methods unto checker, given (the node statements):
        Define rebuilt as cast listed.
        For each statement in statements's children, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "PullStatement":
                Cast rebuilt's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 2, cast one's with-filled-methods on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)))).
                Skip.
            Done.
            If statement's kind is not "ObjectDefinition":
                Cast rebuilt's add on (statement).
                Skip.
            Done.
            Define owner as cast def-name on (statement).
            Define touched as false.
            Define kept as cast listed.
            For each method in (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s children, repeat:
                If (the entry for "{owner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1))}" in one's generic-methods) is not void:
                    The touched becomes true.
                Done.
                Otherwise:
                    Cast kept's add on (method).
                Done.
            Done.
            For each each-filling in one's filled-methods, repeat:
                If each-filling's owner is owner:
                    The touched becomes true.
                    Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (each-filling's method, 1)).
                    Define present as false.
                    For each method in kept's children, repeat:
                        If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) is name, the present becomes true.
                    Done.
                    If present is false, cast kept's add on (each-filling's method).
                Done.
            Done.
            If touched, cast rebuilt's add on (cast with-field on (statement, 4, kept)).
            Otherwise, cast rebuilt's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Return rebuilt.
    Done.

    /// After everything is checked: the fillings' bodies, checked by a fresh checker on the program
    /// with them spliced in front and the templates taken out. Nothing to do when nothing was filled.
    Bind void or failure to check-fillings unto checker, given (the node program):
        If the number of one's instantiated-functions is 0 and the number of one's filled-methods is 0, return.
        If one's instantiation-depth is not less than 16:
            Return a failure "error\tThat doesn't work: filling in these types never finishes.\n\nA type that fills itself in — directly or through another — has no end. Break the cycle, or hold the inner one behind a 'voidable'.".
        Done.
        Define spliced as cast listed.
        For each filled-function in one's instantiated-functions, repeat:
            Cast spliced's add on (filled-function).
        Done.
        For each statement in (cast one's with-filled-methods on (cast one's without-templates on (program)))'s children, repeat:
            Cast spliced's add on (statement).
        Done.
        Define child as cast fresh-checker on (one's prelude-defs).
        The child's instantiation-depth becomes one's instantiation-depth + 1.
        The child's origins becomes one's origins.
        // ⚠ The templates go with it: a call inside a filled body is a fresh copy of the template's,
        // carries no mark, and is filled there.
        For each pair in one's generic-binds, repeat:
            In child's generic-binds, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes the value of pair.
            In child's templates, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes true.
        Done.
        For each pair in one's generic-methods, repeat:
            In child's generic-methods, the entry for (the key of pair) becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Cast child's check-program on (spliced) or pass the failure off.
    Done.
Done.
